# Spec for tools/riscpkg.py: TORCS.
Package: TORCS
Section: Games
Priority: Optional
Licence: Free
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Standards-Version: 0.4.0
Environment: arm32, vfpv3
Depends: MesaLibs (>= 20.3.5.0.21), SharedUnixLibrary (>= 1.16), ARMEABISupport, RISC3D
Components: Apps.Games.!TORCS (Movable LookAt)
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-torcs
Description: The Open Racing Car Simulator, a 3D racing game
 OpenGL racing in a desktop window or full screen, with nine tracks and
 Debian's free cars. With RISC3D it draws on a Pi 4's GPU (and under
 RISC OS on Linux); otherwise in software, about 10 frames a second on a
 Pi 4. Loads OpenGL, SDL 2 and OpenAL from MesaLibs. Needs a fast ARMv7
 machine with NEON and about 64 MB free.
Build-Map: !TORCS -> Apps/Games/!TORCS
Build-Untyped: auto
Build-Notice: TORCS, packaged for PackMan from the release zip on
 https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-torcs/releases
 .
 TORCS 1.3.7 (Debian's torcs 1.3.7+dfsg) is under the GNU GPL version
 2 or later; its data and libraries keep their own licences. Licences
 follow.
Build-Copyright: !TORCS/Licences
Build-Copyright: !TORCS/PThreadTicker-Licence
